      "content": "It's completely understandable to feel that way when the struggle seems endless and the solutions feel hollow. When everything feels broken, the idea of fixing it can feel impossible, like trying to patch a dam with a teacup. Perhaps instead of trying to fix everything, you could focus on finding one tiny, small thing that brings even a moment of quiet relief. Sometimes, the goal isn't to fix the whole machine, but just to find a place where you can rest for a minute.",
